R2.3 STANDING SEMANTIC-DELEGATION AUTHORITY — CONSOLIDATED CURRENT BOUNDARY.

Preserve all previously approved R2.3 permissions, restrictions, immutable source contracts, authority boundaries and audit history.

This instruction consolidates the standing delegation already granted for isolated feature000 formal/reference R2.3 work, including:
- persistence/durability/source-association;
- EC_DURABLE_COMMIT_BINDING;
- MISSING_CONCRETE_SEED_EVIDENCE_VERIFIER;
- and the explicit existing-validator seed-contribution/signing purpose authorized below.

It does not reopen R1/R2.1/R2.2, does not authorize production integration or full R3, and does not itself establish R2.3 closure, recovery correctness or Formal GO.

GENERAL R2.3 DELEGATION

The orchestrator is authorized to design, select, implement, prove, review and qualify the minimal deterministic formal/reference contracts necessary to complete the already authorized R2.3 source/recovery relation without returning for another human decision merely because another missing binding, representation, persistence association, provenance relation, history association, deterministic verifier, deterministic derivation rule or formal/reference statement format must be made explicit.

For delegated classes, prior instructions requiring a specification-only document followed by STOP and a second human semantic-selection decision are superseded.

The orchestrator must still record every selected contract explicitly and immutably before relying on it, but it need not request another Pending decision if the selected solution remains completely inside this authority envelope.

Within isolated feature000 formal/reference R2.3 the orchestrator may:

- inspect and compose all already approved immutable contracts and exact original-source evidence;
- determine that an existing approved contract applies where an explicit applicability argument establishes that fact;
- when approved contracts underdetermine a required R2.3 relation, select one minimal deterministic future-generation formal/reference contract within this envelope;
- introduce the minimum formal/reference fields, schema versions, canonical encodings, identifiers, hashes, source relations, statement kinds, guards and proof machinery necessary to express that contract;
- implement codecs, parsers, checkers, source validators, model guards, fixtures, generators and formal/reference tests;
- construct Lean/TLA/refinement proofs and supporting helper lemmas;
- revise technical details when proof, review or qualification reveals an error, provided the corrected semantics remain inside this authority envelope;
- perform ordinary technical decomposition without further human approval;
- run applicable source/model/refinement/mutant/compatibility/qualification gates and ordinary two-process reviews;
- continue R2.3 composition after successful component qualification instead of stopping merely because an intermediate contract or component has been completed.

Every delegated semantic resolution must be explicit, immutable-source-bound and auditable. Record exact source inputs, selected rule, materially relevant alternatives, rationale, compatibility consequences, affected source/model/reference/proof artifacts and qualification evidence.

A semantic choice must not be hidden inside a theorem premise, helper definition, trusted callback, generated fixture, prevalidated input or opaque success predicate.

EC PERSISTENCE / DURABILITY DELEGATION

For the already identified EC persistence/durability boundary, the orchestrator may within the isolated formal/reference model:

- define the exact persisted formal/reference object binding original E/seed bytes, original event/cut and complete computed P0/P1;
- select exact canonical formal/reference bytes, identifiers, hashes, schema fields/versions and source relations necessary for that binding;
- define append, durability barrier, commit and expose ordering using already approved storage/durability authority and primitives;
- define deterministic incomplete/crash/replay/conflict interpretation;
- preserve and formally bind original physical slots, public vote ordinals, object identities, retries, every retained source occurrence and complete lineage;
- introduce the minimum isolated formal/reference persistence envelope or record representation necessary to express and prove that semantics;
- implement and qualify its codecs/checkers/model guards/fixtures/Lean/TLA/refinement machinery;
- select among multiple admissible representations the minimal deterministic alternative that reuses the greatest amount of already approved authority and does not claim legacy production compatibility.

No further Pending decision is required merely because the selected formal/reference persistence representation or byte layout did not previously exist.

SEED EVIDENCE VERIFIER / DERIVATION DELEGATION

The checkpoint 46f5acff seed-source audit establishes the source boundary for this work. Reuse its exact immutable corpus/source references; do not repeat the same audit without substantive new evidence.

The orchestrator is authorized to design, select, implement, prove and qualify the minimal deterministic concrete seed evidence verifier and seed derivation/source-binding contract necessary to discharge MISSING_CONCRETE_SEED_EVIDENCE_VERIFIER without another human Pending decision, subject to this authority envelope.

The orchestrator may:

- bind exact original reveal/beacon/transcript evidence bytes and every retained source occurrence to the fixed-epoch enrolled Snapshot Provenance Profile v1;
- define exact original accepted seed evidence/transcript fields;
- define canonical/signable preimages and domain separation;
- define exact context binding to validator identity, validator epoch, ISC consensus body b, round/context and original event/cut;
- define the deterministic verification algorithm;
- define deterministic evidence acceptance, selection, ordering and duplicate handling;
- define missing, invalid and incomplete evidence behavior without excluding lawful histories;
- define the exact deterministic seed_id derivation from authorized original evidence and context;
- preserve every original signer/object/cut/history occurrence and complete downstream lineage;
- introduce the minimum isolated formal/reference schema fields, canonical encodings, hashes, codecs, checkers, model guards, fixtures and Lean/TLA/refinement machinery necessary to implement and prove the rule;
- select among admissible designs the minimal deterministic contract that introduces the least new semantics and maximally reuses approved authority;
- revise technical details when proof or review identifies an error while remaining inside this envelope;
- run applicable source/model/refinement/mutant/compatibility gates and ordinary reviews and then continue R2.3 composition.

Do not use public ExpectedSeedValue, successful downstream EC, successful FinalizeEC/Next, custody, hash equality, TLS transport, durable=true, a supplied certificate or another downstream-success observation as its own seed authority or verifier.

EXISTING-VALIDATOR SEED-PURPOSE AUTHORITY DELEGATION

The same already enrolled fixed-epoch validator identities, authenticated through the existing approved validator epoch / independently provisioned key / configuration authority, are explicitly authorized to act as the seed-contribution/signing authority for one minimal concrete bias-resistant post-ISC seed protocol in isolated future-generation feature000 formal/reference work.

This is an explicit additional purpose of the already enrolled validator authority.

It does NOT claim that historical NSG1, ISC votes, existing vote kinds or their historical signatures previously authenticated seed contributions, reveal messages, beacon messages or arbitrary seed evidence.

Within this specific seed purpose the orchestrator is authorized to select, record, implement, prove, review and qualify the minimum concrete protocol and its evidence-generation, verification and deterministic derivation rules without another human Pending decision.

The orchestrator may:

- define one or more minimum formal/reference seed-contribution/reveal statement kinds necessary for the selected protocol;
- define unique domain separators for those seed-purpose statements;
- define exact canonical signed preimages;
- bind every statement to the existing validator identity and existing authenticated validator public key;
- bind the statement to validator epoch, ISC body b, round/context, original event/cut and exact contribution/evidence bytes;
- define deterministic contribution acceptance, ordering, duplicate/conflict, withholding, missing, invalid and incomplete behavior;
- define the minimum quorum/participation rule required by the selected bias-resistant protocol, provided it does not alter the existing validator membership or reinterpret an existing protocol quorum/certificate as proving seed evidence;
- define deterministic seed derivation from the accepted authenticated evidence;
- preserve every original occurrence, conflicting/invalid/incomplete occurrence and complete downstream lineage;
- introduce the minimum isolated formal/reference codecs, statement schemas, hashes, verifiers, source relations, model guards, fixtures and proof machinery necessary for this seed purpose;
- use existing authenticated validator public keys for this additional explicitly domain-separated purpose;
- select among multiple admissible seed protocols the minimal deterministic construction that introduces the least new semantics and preserves the largest lawful original-source/history domain;
- revise the internal protocol/encoding/derivation details when proof or review discovers an error, while remaining within this authority envelope;
- qualify the exact cryptographic assumptions and their applicability instead of trusting a named adapter or opaque success flag.

Existing vote kinds and their semantics remain unchanged.

Historical signatures must never be reinterpreted, relabelled, migrated or treated as signatures over the newly defined seed-purpose statement.

Where the chosen formal/reference seed protocol requires internal deterministic setup or derived material, that material must be completely derived and verified from already approved authority and authenticated original transcript/context. No independently trusted setup, key source, external entropy authority or external beacon is authorized.

The explicit seed-purpose extension above is NOT considered prohibited repurposing of validator authority. It is the human-approved exception for this one R2.3 seed-purpose class.

No additional Pending decision is required merely because the concrete seed statement kind, canonical preimage, domain separator, deterministic derivation, quorum/participation rule, encoding or formal/reference proof construction must be selected inside this explicit purpose.

SEED CONTRACT EVIDENCE REQUIREMENTS

The selected seed contract must immutably record at minimum:

- exact original source bytes/types;
- validator/key/profile applicability;
- exact seed-purpose statement kinds;
- verification algorithm;
- canonical signed preimages and domain separators;
- validator epoch / ISC b / round / context / event-cut binding;
- contribution acceptance and selection rules;
- ordering, duplicate and conflict behavior;
- missing, invalid, incomplete and withholding behavior;
- deterministic seed derivation algorithm;
- materially relevant alternatives and selection rationale;
- cryptographic assumptions and exact applicability;
- compatibility consequences;
- affected theorem/model/reference/qualification obligations.

AUTHORITY ENVELOPE — NEW HUMAN DECISION REQUIRED OUTSIDE IT

A new Pending decision remains mandatory before any action that would:

- introduce a new trust or authority root;
- introduce a new independently trusted key source;
- introduce a new signer population or change validator membership/epoch;
- introduce new validator keys or another independently trusted setup/key authority;
- assign seed/signing authority to storage peers or another actor class not covered by this explicit existing-validator seed-purpose authorization;
- introduce an external beacon authority, entropy service, VRF authority/service requiring new trust, external oracle or other independent source of truth;
- introduce a factual-history observer or new physical-history source of truth;
- extend an existing authority to a new purpose other than the explicitly authorized existing-validator seed purpose above when its approved semantics do not cover that purpose;
- weaken validator membership/epoch authentication requirements;
- weaken or narrow the approved source/admissible-history domain;
- exclude missing, invalid, duplicate, conflicting, incomplete or withheld original evidence merely to make a proof succeed;
- invent source caps or erase loss/fault/history cases;
- synthesize, discard, truncate, relabel or replace missing original bytes/history with callbacks, fixtures or successful downstream results;
- change Snapshot Provenance Profile v1, EC-SOURCE-STEP-v1, Arithmetic Unit Source Binding v1 or another already selected semantic contract rather than compose the minimum missing binding;
- reinterpret historical vote/signature/certificate/QC bytes as having authenticated new seed-purpose content;
- change existing seed/certificate/QC/signature/WAL/original-object identities beyond consequences explicitly authorized by the new future-generation seed-purpose contract;
- change deployed legacy production semantics or production Init/Next;
- add or change a production WAL record kind;
- add or change production WAL/storage byte encoding;
- change production signing/runtime behavior;
- claim existing legacy histories conform to a future-generation formal/reference contract without independently established evidence;
- choose a concrete production seed, private key, arithmetic quantum, sigma or other deployment/runtime semantic value;
- introduce a new clock, duration, expiry mechanism, network-bootstrap authority, backup authority, membership change or epoch change;
- enable production C++/ABI/Java/sidecar integration, production recovery deployment or arithmetic guard removal;
- weaken any safety, determinism, bias-resistance, witness-independence, source-provenance, compatibility, recovery, review or Formal GO gate;
- reopen R1/R2.1/R2.2 outside their approved original domains;
- change the mandatory R2.3 closure criterion;
- weaken or alter the required substantive content of DeltaReduce.nativeArithmeticRecoveryRefines;
- enter full R3.

Where several candidate contracts remain possible inside this envelope, the orchestrator is authorized to select the minimal deterministic contract that:

1. introduces the least new semantics;
2. reuses the greatest amount of already approved authority and canonical representation;
3. preserves the largest lawful source/history domain;
4. adds the smallest isolated formal/reference surface;
5. preserves the required bias-resistance and witness-independence properties;
6. does not claim legacy or production compatibility without independent evidence.

The selected alternative and rationale must be recorded in immutable evidence. Selection inside this envelope does not require another human decision.

EXECUTION AND CLOSURE RULES

R2.3 remains OPEN until its complete source/state relation, initial/incomplete/ABORT correspondence, retained-history obligations, affected models, proofs and required reviews substantively succeed.

A component PASS, process review, ACK, scope application or delegated semantic selection is not R2.3 closure and is not Formal GO.

R1/R2.1/R2.2 remain CLOSED only for their already established original domains.

No sorry, hidden/circular/public-success axioms, vacuous theorem/domain weakening, opaque accept callbacks, prevalidated-success assumptions or relabelled FAIL/NO_GO are permitted.

Requalify every affected source/model/refinement/mutant/compatibility/review gate required by the resulting semantics. Sequential process reviews are not independent Formal GO attestations.

After substantive reviewed R2.3 closure, continue the already authorized DeltaReduce.nativeArithmeticRecoveryRefines, its axiom audit and applicable formal/refinement/mutant/compatibility/qualification gates.

Full R3 remains forbidden.

Preserve the existing sprint, graph history, assignment/review history, immutable evidence, frozen references and unrelated files.

No reimport, reset, manual graph advancement, fake RESUME/START, duplicate result/review, nginx-qa patch/deploy/restart or other runtime-state manipulation is authorized by this semantic delegation.

ACK changes scope authorization/audit only. It never completes an assignment, approves a review, advances the graph or bypasses another gate.

Existing execution, review and qualification gates remain unchanged. This effective instruction supersedes conflicting historical scope text.

Retained restrictions:
- No production C++/ABI/Java/sidecar integration, production recovery deployment or arithmetic guard removal; exact compatible merged Formal GO remains required. Future feature000 semantic/model changes are only those permitted by the current standing R2.3 semantic-delegation authority and remain isolated formal/reference future-generation semantics, never changes to the deployed legacy generation.
- Preserve existing storage authentication bindings, original signer/object/QC/WAL identities and all retained delivery/source multiplicity except for explicit future-generation consequences authorized by the standing R2.3 contracts. No old-object reinterpretation, migration, relabeling or resigning. New generation pins/hashes must be qualified. No concrete sigma_next or other production deployment semantic value.
- F is forbidden. No factual-history observer, new trust/authority root, hidden source-domain restriction, invented source caps, loss/fault erasure, lineage truncation or replacement of missing bytes/history with successful callbacks, fixtures or downstream-success observations. The revised physical-cut claim remains explicit and is not evidence that the old physical-availability claim passed.
- Preserve fixed-epoch enrolled Snapshot Provenance Profile v1 authority and deployment boundaries: no unenrolled node, validator membership change, epoch change, trusted-volume compromise/rollback, network bootstrap, independently trusted external entropy/source-of-truth service or universal backup format without a new explicit human decision.
- R1/R2.1/R2.2 stay CLOSED for their original domains. R2.3 stays OPEN until substantive implementation, proof, composition and required reviews succeed. Named DeltaReduce.nativeArithmeticRecoveryRefines begins only after substantive reviewed R2.3 closure. Full R3 remains forbidden. No conditional refinement may be portrayed as production GO.
- No sorry, hidden/circular/public-success axioms, vacuous theorem/domain weakening, opaque accept callbacks, prevalidated-success assumptions or relabeled FAIL/NO_GO. Requalify every affected source/model/refinement/mutant/compatibility/review gate required by the selected semantics. Sequential process reviews are not independent Formal GO attestations.
- No new sprint, reimport, reset, manual graph advancement, fake RESUME/START for STOP, duplicate result/review, nginx-qa patch/deploy/restart, subagents, foreign-file changes or frozen-ref rewrites unless separately and explicitly authorized for infrastructure maintenance. Preserve execution/audit history and healthy unrelated services. ACK changes scope authorization/audit only and never advances the graph, completes an assignment, approves a review or bypasses another gate.
- The previously selected EC-SOURCE-STEP-v1 semantics remain authoritative. The orchestrator may compose and qualify the minimum isolated formal/reference EC persistence/durability/source-association contract under the standing delegation. This does not authorize a production WAL kind, production storage encoding, W1 extension, deployed runtime producer change, new trust root or legacy-history conformance claim.
- Seed evidence verifier/derivation selection, implementation and proof are delegated within the standing R2.3 authority. The orchestrator may select and implement the minimal deterministic formal/reference verifier and seed derivation contract using approved original evidence/context and the explicitly authorized existing-validator seed-purpose authority.
- The already enrolled fixed-epoch validators and their already authenticated validator public keys are explicitly authorized for the additional isolated future-generation formal/reference seed-contribution/signing purpose defined by the standing instruction. This is not authority to reinterpret historical ISC/vote/NSG1 signatures as seed signatures. New seed-purpose statements require explicit unique domains and canonical preimages.
- No implicit reuse of NSG1, ISC vote signatures, certificate signatures or another historical signature type as a seed/beacon protocol is permitted. Historical signatures may not be relabelled or treated as covering content they did not sign.
- No new Pending decision is required for ordinary protocol/statement/encoding/preimage/domain-separation/quorum/ordering/derivation/proof choices inside the explicitly authorized existing-validator seed purpose, provided validator identities, epoch membership and authenticated validator keys remain unchanged and no independent trust source is introduced.
- A new Pending decision remains mandatory before introducing a new trust/authority root, independently trusted key/setup source, new signer population, new validator keys, external beacon/entropy authority, factual-history observer, external oracle or other independent source of truth; before extending another actor class to a new authority purpose outside the explicit existing-validator seed-purpose delegation; before weakening validator/epoch authentication, bias-resistance or witness-independence; before narrowing the lawful source/admissible-history domain; before changing deployed production semantics, production Init/Next, production signing/runtime behavior or production WAL/storage encoding; before reinterpreting historical signatures/objects; before choosing concrete production seed/private-key/arithmetic/sigma values; before weakening any safety, determinism, provenance, compatibility, recovery, review or Formal GO gate; or before entering full R3.
- The orchestrator must not silently repurpose an existing authority outside the explicit existing-validator seed-purpose exception. Applicability of any existing key, validator authority, storage authority or configuration authority must remain explicit and source-bound.
- Dependent R2.3 composition may continue after each delegated contract has been explicitly recorded, implemented, proved and passed its applicable ordinary review/qualification gates. No additional Pending decision is required merely to select another minimal deterministic formal/reference binding, persistence association, verifier, derivation rule, provenance relation, history-association rule or seed-purpose protocol detail that stays inside the standing delegation envelope.
- Every delegated semantic choice must remain explicit, immutable-source-bound and auditable, including exact source inputs, selected rule, materially relevant alternatives, rationale, cryptographic assumptions where applicable, compatibility consequences and affected qualification. It must not be hidden as a theorem premise, helper definition, trusted callback, fixture assumption or prevalidated input.
- If multiple solutions satisfy the delegated envelope, select the minimal deterministic solution that introduces the least new semantics, reuses the greatest amount of approved authority and canonical representation, preserves the largest lawful source/history domain, preserves required bias-resistance and witness-independence, and adds the smallest isolated formal/reference surface.
- The standing delegation itself is not evidence that R2.3 is correct or closed and is not Formal GO. Component PASS, process review, scope application or ACK likewise does not establish closure.
- After substantive reviewed R2.3 closure, continue the already authorized DeltaReduce.nativeArithmeticRecoveryRefines, its axiom audit and applicable formal/refinement/mutant/compatibility/qualification gates. Production integration and full R3 remain outside this authority.

Existing execution, review and qualification gates remain unchanged. This effective instruction supersedes conflicting historical scope text.

